intent: Bring the run's draft commit e70e5c8 (untrusted draft) onto a session worktree, keep the debug suite timeout at 120s (the run-startup-regression runner needed timeoutMs instead), keep the R2 decisions in run-goal.md, then verify, review and finish. Replaces task-e46fdfb2, whose surface revision history outgrew the 64 KiB review packet.
criteria:
- ac1-rule-discovery: Rule files .agent-ops-escapes/rules/<id>.json ({id, escape, label, trigger {paths, tokens}, expand {paths, queries}, noExclude}) are strictly schema-validated with no field that removes a query, adds an exclusion or relaxes a gate; an invalid rule fails closed as review NOT_RUN ESCAPE_RULE_INVALID and a symlinked rules directory or rule file as ESCAPE_RULE_UNSAFE. The surface gate applies a rule only when the task diff matches a trigger path glob or contains a trigger token; a fired rule's expand hits (path globs over tracked files plus argv git grep -F queries) must each be in the diff, included, UNKNOWN or excluded, else SURFACE_UNCLASSIFIED, and with noExclude an excluded hit fails as ESCAPE_RULE_NO_EXCLUDE; fires and included/excluded outcomes per rule go to the local log fail-open. Synthetic-repo checks: escape-rule-schema, escape-rule-unsafe, escape-rule-fire, escape-rule-no-fire, escape-rule-no-exclude; all pre-existing runner checks keep passing.
- ac2-escape-proof: A task with an escape-of origin whose primary label is surface, surface-unseen or surface-excluded cannot complete (task complete, worktree finish, completion gate) unless the ledger record names a tracked rule (matching content hash) for that escape whose replay at the escaped commit fires on that commit's diff and whose expand hits cover every missed path present at that commit, else ESCAPE_RULE_UNPROVEN; criteria/verify labels require the declared promoted check (runnerId:checkId) to be a redCheckId of a proven behavioral criterion of this task, else ESCAPE_RULE_UNPROVEN, and print a config proposal without writing .agent-ops/config.json; scenario/review/requirement/flagged/out-of-model record an unproven lesson with a reason and do not block. No review or test runs at the escaped commit. Checks: escape-proof-surface, escape-proof-criteria, escape-proof-lesson.
- ac3-rule-backtest: Every rule used as proof is backtested by matching its trigger against the diffs of the last 200 first-parent commits (argv git only); a fire rate above 30% blocks completion as ESCAPE_RULE_TOO_BROAD; the backtest is time-budgeted (over budget records SURFACE_BUDGET_EXCEEDED and blocks, never a silent pass) and cached by HEAD and rule hash; fires, commits and rate are stored in the ledger record. Checks: escape-backtest-broad, escape-backtest-budget-cache.
- ac4-escape-fix: task create|revise --escape-of <commit> --escape-label <label> --escape-fix <fix-commit> binds fix into the origin and contract, derives missed paths from the fix commit's diff (fix^..fix) instead of the task diff, and goes through the same proof and backtest; synthetic checks reproduce a sibling-page omission and an alternate-entry-path omission, each ESCAPE_RULE_UNPROVEN without a rule and proven with it. Checks: escape-fix-sibling-page, escape-fix-alternate-entry.
- ac5-escapes-report: agent-ops escapes [--json] is read-only and fails open: it reports per-gate misses from the tracked ledger and catches from local-log gate-catch events with time windows, origin mix, link-state mix with reasons, per-rule fire/included/excluded counts and retirement candidates, as raw counts with n and insufficient-data when n < 10, and never writes files. docs/en/spec and docs/zh-TW/spec plus the managed DEBUG text describe R2 rules, proof, backtest, --escape-fix and the report, and state that they supersede surface.aliases and surface stats. Checks: escape-report, escape-r2-spec-docs.
